root_cause_investigation:
  shell_process: "Robert's PowerShell pid 14740 (started 13:33:13 local, parent AapWin.Host.exe pid 4368 running as SYSTEM, cmd 'powershell.exe -NoLogo -ExecutionPolicy Bypass') runs as aapw-a20u19 with CWD and AAP_WORKSPACE = sandbox home, AAP_SESSION=aap-agent-20, AAP_UNIT_ID=19, but USERPROFILE=C:\Users\aapw-a20u19, APPDATA/LOCALAPPDATA under that profile, no HOME, CODEX_HOME or CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR. Path starts with the sandbox .npm-global. It still carries CIEL_RUNTIME_UPDATE_BRANCH=nightly (started before the deletion)."
  aap_win_db: "Copied aap-win.db: containers id 19 (windows-sandbox sbx-u19) env_vars '{}', home_dir null; sandbox_accounts aapw-a20u19 home_directory = sandbox home; assignment provision_log shows no CLI runtime or provision script; agents id 20 session_restore_command \"$env:CIEL_RUNTIME_SKIP_MENU='1'; ciel-runtime --ca-runtime last --continue\"."
  migration: "apply-state.py and apply-delta.py copy Linux /home/robert-ai data into the sandbox home and relocate paths inside Codex SQLite/config; neither sets environment. Only activate-paths.py bridges the paths, by writing .npm-global\ciel-runtime.cmd and codex.cmd wrappers (CODEX_HOME, CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR, CIEL_RUNTIME_LAUNCH_CWD)."
  ciel_code: "origin/nightly reads no AAP_* variable; npm-bin sets neither CODEX_HOME nor CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR; config dir = CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR or %APPDATA%\ciel-runtime, Codex home = CODEX_HOME or Path.home()\.codex."
  finding: "The sandbox home relocation exists only as wrapper files inside npm's global bin directory, which npm regenerates on every global install of the package; the session launcher (aap-win) and ciel-runtime provide no other route to the sandbox paths."
restore (user-approved):
  precondition: "Another npm install --global github:OneCielAI/ciel-runtime#nightly ran 13:52:47-13:53:56 local (exit 0) and rewrote the shims at 13:53:55; no npm install process running at write time."
  backup: ".migration-20260930\pre-restore-20261001\ciel-runtime.cmd (363 B) and ciel-runtime.ps1 (957 B), the npm shims."
  written: ".npm-global\ciel-runtime.cmd = activate-paths.py wrapper (CODEX_HOME, CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR, CIEL_RUNTIME_LAUNCH_CWD, cd /d home, call node_modules\.bin\ciel-runtime.cmd); .npm-global\ciel-runtime.ps1 sets the same three for the call only, Push/Pop-Location to home, calls node_modules\.bin\ciel-runtime.cmd, restores the caller's values. 13:54:54 local; ps1 parse errors 0."
  verified:
    - "With robert's Path, PowerShell resolves ciel-runtime to .npm-global\ciel-runtime.ps1 first (then .cmd)."
    - "Probe copies of both wrappers (final call replaced by an env echo): CWD = sandbox home, CODEX_HOME, CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR, CIEL_RUNTIME_LAUNCH_CWD = sandbox paths, args passed (--continue), exit code passed; caller shell afterwards unchanged (cwd and variables)."
    - "Installed ciel code with those values: CONFIG_DIR = sandbox .config\ciel-runtime; Codex DB = sandbox .codex\state_5.sqlite (exists, threads 4); workspace id e87f37af3b3a -> symlink to workspaces\51c584b37985 whose config has workspace_mcp servers walkie, walkie_transcripts."
  not_verified: "A real ciel-runtime launch in robert's window (needs robert's session; robert's shell pid 14740 still carries the old process environment including CIEL_RUNTIME_UPDATE_BRANCH, which no installed code reads)."
  limit: "Any later npm install -g of ciel-runtime into this prefix rewrites both files again."
